# Grid A — S7 Measurement scalar (line count across directory)
#
# Targets: generic scenario + ShapeValue + measurement-scalar
# carve-out (session 6) that strips the 3-layer citation gate and
# renders Raw Tool Outputs from Turn A into the Turn B prompt.
#
# Ground truth: actual line count depends on repo state and will
# drift; EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX pins only that a 4+ digit number
# appears (any non-trivial codebase gives ≥1000 lines in
# internal/tool). This is the pattern session 6 targeted — LLM must
# reach a wc -l / find-pipe output from the exec_command tool and
# quote the number rather than estimate.
#
# Negative anchors block the classic failure modes: "approximately",
# "roughly", "estimated" — all signs the LLM guessed rather than
# executed.
ID="s7a"
NAME="measurement scalar — total .go LOC under internal/tool (non-test)"
QUESTION="internal/tool 目录下所有 .go 文件（不含 _test.go）的总行数是多少？请给出准确数字。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="internal/tool"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="approximately roughly estimated"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit (post_v2_runtime_gap_remediation):
# previous regex `[0-9]{4,}` accepted ANY 4+ digit number — a false
# positive: an answer like "approximately 1234" would pass. Ground
# truth `wc -l internal/tool/*.go` (excluding _test.go) = 23,828 at
# this snapshot. Narrow to the 5-digit 2x,xxx range so the answer
# must be in the correct magnitude (small drift over time fits;
# 4-digit / 30K+ guesses fail). Both `23828` and `23,828` formats
# accepted.
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b2[0-9],?[0-9]{3}\b"
